<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pacific War</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pacific War was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> fought in Asia and the Pacific from 1941 to 1945, chiefly between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. After the US <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/us-oil-embargo-against-japan">oil embargo</a> of 1941, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> launched a wide offensive and by mid-1942 controlled a vast area. Japan's defeat in 1945 ended the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pacific-war.jpg" alt="Pacific War" width="320" height="243" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joe Rosenthal · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raising_the_Flag_on_Iwo_Jima,_larger_-_edit1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
